var documenterSearchIndex = {"docs":
[{"category":"section","location":"connectome/#Connectome-substrate","page":"Connectome substrate","text":"A unified, persisted, manifest-driven representation of the FAFB v783 adult Drosophila connectome on the MORK substrate, and the Fig-6 information-flow model (Dorkenwald, Schlegel et al., Nature 2024) run over it. Lives in examples/connectome/.\n\nIt is the first concrete instance of the PRIMUS world-modeling architecture (\"World Modeling in Hyperon for PRIMUS\", Goertzel 2025): a real heterogeneous graph organized into the world-model Spaces, all co-resolving on one key — the neuron root_id — with the raw data kept immutable as evidence. The conceptual App+Common mapping is in docs/CONNECTOME_MULTISPACE.md; this page documents the implemented substrate.","title":"Connectome substrate"},{"category":"section","location":"connectome/#The-Spaces","page":"Connectome substrate","text":"Space Atom Source Role\nS_ent (neuron <id> <flow> <super_class> <class> <sub_class> <side>) classification.csv.gz (139,256 neurons) identity / ontology. For afferent neurons class is the sensory modality — info-flow seeds are derived by querying this Space, not hand-listed.\nS_rule (syn <pre> <post> <Σsyn_count>) connections_princeton.csv.gz (5.34 M rows → 3,732,460 unique edges) the wiring.\nS_map (skel-br <id> <bid> <st> <sx> <sy> <sz> <et> <ex> <ey> <ez> <len> <rad> <n>) 139,273 SWC skeletons → 28 branch-decomposed .act shards spatial morphology (branch endpoints, cable length, radius).\nS_evid the raw 31 GB SWC files sk_lod1_783_healed/<id>.swc immutable evidence. Provenance is root_id → <id>.swc — already implicit in every skel-br atom (no CID field, no re-import).\n\nEvery Space keys on the same root_id, so one id resolves its class (S_ent), morphology (S_map), synapses (S_rule), and source file (S_evid).","title":"The Spaces"},{"category":"section","location":"connectome/#Design-—-MORK-canonical,-no-technical-debt","page":"Connectome substrate","text":"One .act per Space (canonical per-Space tries), cold-mmap'd on use (act_open_mmap, ~0 RAM) — built once, instant thereafter. No /tmp staging, no re-ingest per run.\nManifest-driven paths (manifest.jl) — single source of truth, ENV-overridable (CONNECTOME_DATA_ROOT / CONNECTOME_STORE / CONNECTOME_SKEL_DIR / MORK_PROJECT); no hardcoded absolute paths.\nReads via the documented zipper algebra (read_zipper_at_path + prefix-narrowed walks over the .act snapshot — the sanctioned high-speed read path for relational reachability).\nDerive, don't pre-bake: seeds come from an S_ent match, not a text file.","title":"Design — MORK-canonical, no technical debt"},{"category":"section","location":"connectome/#Files-(examples/connectome/)","page":"Connectome substrate","text":"File What\nmanifest.jl resolved paths (data root, store, shards, MORK project)\nload_ent.jl classification.csv.gz → S_ent.act; query_seeds(modality)\nload_rule.jl connections.csv.gz → S_rule.act (Julia-side aggregation, no awk/TSV)\nload_map.jl S_map accessor over the skeleton shards; query_skeleton, neuron_morphology, evid_swc_path\ninfo_flow.jl the Fig-6 flow over the persisted store: info_flow, validate, all_modalities\n\nCompanion artifacts: InfoFlow.metta / InfoFlowMS.metta / InfoFlowFast.metta (pure-MeTTa exec-calculus models — a different, interpreter-based approach), import_fafb_skeletons.jl (the S_map importer), extract_{fafb,banc,flywire}_subset.sh (subset/oracle generators; BANC + FlyWire are future cross-species runs), STAGE2_RESULTS.md.","title":"Files (examples/connectome/)"},{"category":"section","location":"connectome/#Usage","page":"Connectome substrate","text":"Run inside the MORK project's warm REPL (the substrate uses raw MORK/PathMap):\n\ninclude(\"examples/connectome/info_flow.jl\")\nusing .ConnectomeManifest\nm = ConnectomeManifest.manifest()\n\n# Build the store (idempotent; first S_rule build ~4 min, then instant cold-mmap):\nConnectomeManifest.ensure_store()\nopen_store(m)                       # builds/opens S_rule.act + S_ent.act\n\n# Single-modality info-flow (seeds derived from S_ent):\nseeds, ranks = info_flow(m, \"thermosensory\")\n\n# Regression: zipper-frontier flow == independent in-Julia oracle, from the store:\nvalidate(m, \"thermosensory\")        # → 0 rank-mismatches\n\n# Fig-6 d/e across all 7 afferent modalities on one shared connectome:\nall_modalities(m)                   # per-modality rank histograms + Jaccard overlap\n\n# Cross-Space resolution by neuron id:\ninclude(\"examples/connectome/load_map.jl\")\nneuron_morphology(m, \"720575940611720362\")   # branches, cable length, S_evid path","title":"Usage"},{"category":"section","location":"connectome/#Validation","page":"Connectome substrate","text":"Build: S_rule.act reproduces the 5.34 M → 3,732,460 unique-edge aggregation.\nFlow vs oracle: thermosensory reaches 367 neurons with rank-1 = 46, and the zipper-frontier flow matches an independent naive-rescan oracle node-for-node (0 mismatches) — both re-derived from the persisted store.\nFig-6 d/e: all 7 modalities run on one shared connectome; the cross-modality Jaccard matrix shows the expected biology (e.g. AN↔mechanosensory ≈ 0.41, thermo↔gustatory = 0.0).\nCross-Space join: all 29/29 thermosensory seeds resolve in S_ent, S_map (e.g. 214 branches / 601,722 nm), S_rule, and S_evid on the same root_id.","title":"Validation"},{"category":"section","location":"connectome/#Data-and-citation","page":"Connectome substrate","text":"Real FlyWire/Codex FAFB v783 exports (CC-BY-NC). Cite Dorkenwald, Schlegel et al., Nature 2024 (\"Neuronal wiring diagram of an adult brain\") for any published result. Raw data is gitignored; not redistributed here.","title":"Data & citation"},{"category":"section","location":"#MeTTaCore.jl","page":"Home","text":"MeTTaCore is the canonical standalone MeTTa interpreter of the CognitiveSubstratesAI stack, running on the MORK byte-trie substrate. Evaluation is eager and single-result; numbers are Float64. Dispatch is three-tier: special forms → grounded operations → rule rewriting.\n\nusing MeTTaCore\nspace = new_core_space()\nef = e -> to_sexpr(eval_metta(from_sexpr(e), space))\nregister_all_primitives!(); _register_atom_ops!(ef); load_stdlib!(space)\n\nrun_metta(\"!(+ 2 3)\", space)            # => 5\nrun_metta(\"!(import! &self (library MOSES))\", space)","title":"MeTTaCore.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#Algorithm-library","page":"Home","text":"Cognitive algorithms live in lib/ as MeTTa, loaded on demand via !(import! &self (library <Name>)):\n\nMOSES — Meta-Optimizing Semantic Evolutionary Search (competent program evolution: representation → knob-building → boolean reduct → getCandidate → scoring → hill-climb → metapopulation search). End-to-end verified to learn boolean functions.\nPLN — Probabilistic Logic Networks core logic.\nECAN — Economic Attention Networks.\nMetaMo — motivational framework.\nActPC-Chem / ActPC-Geom — Active Predictive Coding.","title":"Algorithm library"},{"category":"section","location":"#Design-notes","page":"Home","text":"In-repo design and architecture documents live under docs/ (algorithm-library governance, the primitive-surface audit, the multi-space/connectome architecture, and per-algorithm specs). The cross-cutting research corpus and source-paper map live in the shared CognitiveSubstratesAI/docs repository.\n\nnote: Note\nThe API reference is a work in progress; this page will grow @autodocs sections as the public surface stabilizes.","title":"Design notes"}]
}
